
1. Modules & Importing — The Tool Crib System
In Python, thousands of ready-made tools live in modules. The import keyword acts as the requisition slip to sign out tools for your program.
2. Traceback Species #3 — NameError
 * Cause: Occurs when attempting to use a tool/function that was never signed out or defined (e.g., calling sqrt(50) without importing it or without using math.sqrt()).
 * Error Diagnosis Comparison:
   * TypeError: Wrong materials welded together (e.g., adding int to str).
   * ValueError: Hopeless input value provided to a function.
   * NameError: Tool not drawn/imported or variable name unrecognized.
3. Key Toolboxes & Functions
Math Toolkit (math)
 * Ceiling Thinking (math.ceil): Rounds up to the next integer.
   * Shop Logic: "Boxes I must order". For 137 / 12 = 11.41, math.ceil(137/12) gives 12 boxes needed.
 * Floor Thinking (// Operator): Rounds down to the whole integer.
   * Shop Logic: "Boxes I can fill". 137 // 12 gives 11 full boxes.
Random Simulation Toolkit (random)
 * random.randint(a, b): Generates random whole integers between a and b inclusive (e.g., random.randint(1, 6) for a die roll).
 * random.uniform(a, b): Generates random floating-point decimals within range (a, b) (e.g., random.uniform(24.95, 25.05) for shop tolerance testing).
